; Labeled-call family, 4 of 4. Every label given is valid and unique; `:t`
; is simply absent. Labels are not optional-by-omission — a declared
; parameter list is a complete signature, so a well-formed subset of it is
; still an incomplete call.
;
; This is the case the other three deliberately do not also produce: they
; each stop at the malformed label rather than going on to report the call
; as incomplete, so this code needs a document whose labels are otherwise
; clean to fire at all.
(lerp :from 0 :to 10)
